{%- comment -%}
  BBC New Design (2026) — "Our Story / About" page. Single self-contained section.
  Built from the Claude Design handoff (about.html) and scoped under
  .bbc-rd / .bbc-rd-about via bbc-redesign-2026.css so it cannot affect other
  sections. Real BBC content (milestones, founder voice, model, recognition)
  folded in from the existing theme sections + page.our-story-2.json.

  Content policy (hard rules):
    - Prisons MAY be named (policy changed by James 2026-06-17). What is still forbidden is
      linking a NAMED OR IDENTIFIABLE PERSON to a named prison. This matters for imagery as
      much as copy: of the five Lowdham photos in Files, three show identifiable faces beside
      a wall reading "HM Prison Lowdham Grange" and must never be used here. Only
      bbc-rd-prison-empty.jpg (no people) is safe. Minors need a release — the school photos
      in Files are close-up identifiable children and are NOT usable.
    - Only source-of-truth figures are hardcoded as defaults
      (4,000+ since 2012 · 90% prison course completion
       · 45 countries · frame kits from £375 · Bamboo Mobility Project CIC, Reg 16257348).
      The CIC is the TRADING entity as well as the programme one; BBC London Ltd holds IP and
      the university/R&D work (confirmed by James 2026-07-31 — the vault had this reversed).
    - Image fields fall back to bundled bbc-rd-*.jpg assets until real photos are set.

  Structure: full-bleed hero → origin band (founder-at-work photo) → "fourteen years, one
  through-line" culm timeline → "a shop and a mission, one engine" mitred-joint model →
  three values (each with a real instance) → six story cards → recognition (press logos +
  dimensioned stats) → final CTA. Every string/image/link/row is editable via {% schema %}.

  The four fabrication-drawing devices (joint, dimension callout, culm, cross-section) are
  documented at the top of their CSS block in assets/bbc-redesign-2026.css, including why
  each is a new class or opt-in modifier rather than a restyle.
{%- endcomment -%}


{%- liquid
  assign crumb_home = section.settings.crumb_home_url | default: '/'
  assign cta1 = section.settings.cta1_url | default: '/pages/bicycle-frame-building-workshop'
  assign cta2 = section.settings.cta2_url | default: '/pages/impact'
-%}

<div class="bbc-rd bbc-rd-about">

  {%- comment -%} ---------- HERO ---------- {%- endcomment -%}
  <header class="rd-hero">
    <div class="rd-bg">
      {%- if section.settings.hero_image != blank -%}
        <img src="{{ section.settings.hero_image | image_url: width: 1600 }}" srcset="{{ section.settings.hero_image | image_url: width: 800 }} 800w, {{ section.settings.hero_image | image_url: width: 1200 }} 1200w, {{ section.settings.hero_image | image_url: width: 1600 }} 1600w, {{ section.settings.hero_image | image_url: width: 2000 }} 2000w, {{ section.settings.hero_image | image_url: width: 2600 }} 2600w" sizes="100vw" alt="{{ section.settings.hero_image_alt | default: 'The Bamboo Bicycle Club workshop and community' | escape }}" width="{{ section.settings.hero_image.width }}" height="{{ section.settings.hero_image.height }}" fetchpriority="high" loading="eager">
      {%- else -%}
        <img src="{{ section.settings.hero_fallback | default: 'bbc-rd-cohort.jpg' | asset_url }}" alt="{{ section.settings.hero_image_alt | default: 'The Bamboo Bicycle Club workshop and community' | escape }}" width="1200" height="800" fetchpriority="high" loading="eager">
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>
    <div class="rd-scrim"></div>
    <div class="rd-inner">
      <div class="rd-wrap">
        <nav class="rd-crumb">
          <a href="{{ crumb_home }}">{{ section.settings.crumb_home_label | default: 'Home' }}</a>
          <span class="rd-sep">/</span>
          <span class="rd-here">{{ section.settings.crumb_here | default: 'Our Story' }}</span>
        </nav>
        {%- if section.settings.hero_eyebrow != blank -%}<span class="rd-frame-label rd-c-lime">{{ section.settings.hero_eyebrow }}</span>{%- endif -%}
        <h1 class="rd-mt2 rd-mw-18ch">{{ section.settings.hero_title }}</h1>
        {%- if section.settings.hero_lede != blank -%}<div class="rd-lede">{{ section.settings.hero_lede }}</div>{%- endif -%}
      </div>
    </div>
  </header>

  {%- comment -%} ---------- MISSION INTRO ---------- {%- endcomment -%}
  <section class="rd-pad">
    <div class="rd-wrap">
      {%- comment -%} The origin band carried 107 words and NO image — the biggest storytelling
         gap on the page. The field research is specific here: one photo of a founder WORKING,
         not portrait-posed, beside the origin story. Asymmetric split (1.55/1), never 50/50,
         per FORMULA §8. {%- endcomment -%}
      <div class="rd-origin">
        <div>
          {%- if section.settings.intro_eyebrow != blank -%}<span class="rd-eyebrow">{{ section.settings.intro_eyebrow }}</span>{%- endif -%}
          <h2 class="rd-reveal rd-mw-18ch">{{ section.settings.intro_title }}</h2>
          {%- if section.settings.intro_body_1 != blank -%}<p class="rd-lede rd-mt2 rd-maxw">{{ section.settings.intro_body_1 }}</p>{%- endif -%}
          {%- if section.settings.intro_body_2 != blank -%}<p class="rd-lede rd-mt2 rd-maxw">{{ section.settings.intro_body_2 }}</p>{%- endif -%}
          {%- if section.settings.intro_quote != blank -%}
            <div class="rd-pull rd-mt4 rd-reveal">
              <p class="rd-q">{{ section.settings.intro_quote }}</p>
              {%- if section.settings.intro_cite != blank -%}<cite>{{ section.settings.intro_cite }}</cite>{%- endif -%}
            </div>
          {%- endif -%}
        </div>
        {%- assign _oi = section.settings.intro_image -%}
        {%- if section.settings.intro_image_pic != blank or _oi != blank -%}
          <figure class="rd-reveal" style="margin:0">
            <div class="rd-origin__media">
              {%- if section.settings.intro_image_pic != blank -%}
                <img src="{{ section.settings.intro_image_pic | image_url: width: 900 }}" srcset="{{ section.settings.intro_image_pic | image_url: width: 480 }} 480w, {{ section.settings.intro_image_pic | image_url: width: 900 }} 900w" sizes="(max-width:840px) 92vw, 380px" alt="{{ section.settings.intro_image_alt | escape }}" loading="lazy" width="{{ section.settings.intro_image_pic.width }}" height="{{ section.settings.intro_image_pic.height }}">
              {%- elsif _oi contains '//' -%}
                <img src="{{ _oi }}&width=900" srcset="{{ _oi }}&width=480 480w, {{ _oi }}&width=900 900w" sizes="(max-width:840px) 92vw, 380px" alt="{{ section.settings.intro_image_alt | escape }}" loading="lazy" width="900" height="1125">
              {%- else -%}
                <img src="{{ _oi | asset_url }}" alt="{{ section.settings.intro_image_alt | escape }}" loading="lazy" width="900" height="1125">
              {%- endif -%}
            </div>
            {%- if section.settings.intro_caption != blank -%}<figcaption class="rd-origin__cap">{{ section.settings.intro_caption }}</figcaption>{%- endif -%}
          </figure>
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  {%- comment -%} ---------- TIMELINE ---------- {%- endcomment -%}
  <section class="rd-pad rd-dark">
    <div class="rd-wrap">
      {%- if section.settings.tl_eyebrow != blank -%}<span class="rd-eyebrow rd-on-dark">{{ section.settings.tl_eyebrow }}</span>{%- endif -%}
      <h2 class="rd-reveal rd-mw-18ch">{{ section.settings.tl_title }}</h2>
      {%- if section.settings.tl_intro != blank -%}<p class="rd-lede rd-maxw rd-mt2">{{ section.settings.tl_intro }}</p>{%- endif -%}
      {%- comment -%} DEVICE D — the culm. Bamboo grows in segments divided by nodes, and a node
         is exactly what a timeline marker is. The rail sits in the existing grid gap, so no
         track sizes change. .rd-tl is used by this section only. {%- endcomment -%}
      <div class="rd-timeline rd-culm rd-mt4">
        {%- for block in section.blocks -%}{%- if block.type == 'milestone' -%}
          {%- if block.settings.hot -%}{%- assign tl_class = 'rd-tl rd-hot rd-reveal' -%}{%- else -%}{%- assign tl_class = 'rd-tl rd-reveal' -%}{%- endif -%}
          {%- comment -%} The media is a SIBLING of the text, not nested inside it. Stacked, each
             illustrated row cost text + 287px of image = 441px for 29 words, and the band grew to
             25% of the whole page. As a grid sibling the row costs max(text, image) instead.
             Rows with no photo span both columns so there is no dead right column (FORMULA §8 r6). {%- endcomment -%}
          {%- if block.settings.image_pic != blank or block.settings.image != blank -%}
            {%- assign tl_class = tl_class | append: ' rd-tl--media' -%}
          {%- endif -%}
          <div class="{{ tl_class }}" {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>
            <div class="rd-yr">{{ block.settings.year }}</div>
            <div class="rd-tl-body">
              <h3>{{ block.settings.title }}</h3>
              {%- if block.settings.body != blank -%}<p>{{ block.settings.body }}</p>{%- endif -%}
            </div>
            {%- comment -%} Picker OR text, same convention as snippets/bbc-cscard.liquid: a
               string containing '//' is a CDN URL, anything else is a theme asset. {%- endcomment -%}
            {%- if block.settings.image_pic != blank -%}
              <div class="rd-tl-media">
                <img src="{{ block.settings.image_pic | image_url: width: 900 }}" srcset="{{ block.settings.image_pic | image_url: width: 450 }} 450w, {{ block.settings.image_pic | image_url: width: 900 }} 900w" sizes="(max-width:900px) 92vw, 320px" alt="{{ block.settings.image_alt | escape }}" loading="lazy" width="{{ block.settings.image_pic.width }}" height="{{ block.settings.image_pic.height }}">
              </div>
            {%- elsif block.settings.image != blank -%}
              <div class="rd-tl-media">
                {%- if block.settings.image contains '//' -%}
                  <img src="{{ block.settings.image }}&width=900" srcset="{{ block.settings.image }}&width=450 450w, {{ block.settings.image }}&width=900 900w" sizes="(max-width:900px) 92vw, 320px" alt="{{ block.settings.image_alt | escape }}" loading="lazy" width="900" height="563">
                {%- else -%}
                  <img src="{{ block.settings.image | asset_url }}" alt="{{ block.settings.image_alt | escape }}" loading="lazy" width="900" height="563">
                {%- endif -%}
              </div>
            {%- endif -%}
          </div>
        {%- endif -%}{%- endfor -%}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  {%- comment -%} ---------- THE MODEL (split + funding loop) ---------- {%- endcomment -%}
  <section class="rd-split rd-rev">
    <div class="rd-media rd-reveal">
      {%- if section.settings.model_image != blank -%}
        <img src="{{ section.settings.model_image | image_url: width: 1500 }}" alt="{{ section.settings.model_image_alt | default: 'The Bamboo Bicycle Club workshop and community' | escape }}" width="{{ section.settings.model_image.width }}" height="{{ section.settings.model_image.height }}">
      {%- else -%}
        <img src="{{ section.settings.model_fallback | default: 'bbc-rd-workshop.jpg' | asset_url }}" alt="{{ section.settings.model_image_alt | default: 'The Bamboo Bicycle Club workshop and community' | escape }}" width="1500" height="999">
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>
    <div class="rd-txt">
      {%- if section.settings.model_eyebrow != blank -%}<span class="rd-eyebrow">{{ section.settings.model_eyebrow }}</span>{%- endif -%}
      <h2 class="rd-reveal">{{ section.settings.model_title }}</h2>
      {%- if section.settings.model_body != blank -%}<p class="rd-lede rd-mt2">{{ section.settings.model_body }}</p>{%- endif -%}
      {%- comment -%} DEVICE A — the mitred joint. Was .rd-loop: three boxes and two arrows, the
         shape every template ships. A frame is made by mitring tubes so they meet at one joint,
         so the funding model is drawn as that joint: three members, one bind. Deliberately a NEW
         class — .rd-loop is shared with home/product/workshops and must not change. {%- endcomment -%}
      <div class="rd-joint rd-mt3">
        <div class="rd-jt"><span class="rd-tube" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          <span class="rd-mono">{{ section.settings.loop_l1 | default: 'Member 01' }}</span>
          <div class="rd-big">{{ section.settings.loop_s1_big }}</div>
          <div class="rd-sm">{{ section.settings.loop_s1_sm }}</div>
        </div>
        <div class="rd-jt"><span class="rd-tube" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          <span class="rd-mono">{{ section.settings.loop_l2 | default: 'Member 02' }}</span>
          <div class="rd-big">{{ section.settings.loop_s2_big }}</div>
          <div class="rd-sm">{{ section.settings.loop_s2_sm }}</div>
        </div>
        <div class="rd-jt"><span class="rd-tube" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          <span class="rd-mono">{{ section.settings.loop_l3 | default: 'Member 03 · bonded' }}</span>
          <div class="rd-big">{{ section.settings.loop_s3_big }}</div>
          <div class="rd-sm">{{ section.settings.loop_s3_sm }}</div>
        </div>
      </div>
      {%- if section.settings.model_reg != blank -%}<p class="rd-mt3 rd-c-charcoal">{{ section.settings.model_reg }}</p>{%- endif -%}
    </div>
  </section>

  {%- comment -%} ---------- VALUES ---------- {%- endcomment -%}
  <section class="rd-pad rd-paper">
    <div class="rd-wrap">
      <div class="rd-center rd-cmp-84401">
        {%- if section.settings.values_eyebrow != blank -%}<span class="rd-eyebrow">{{ section.settings.values_eyebrow }}</span>{%- endif -%}
        <h2 class="rd-reveal">{{ section.settings.values_title }}</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="rd-grid rd-g3">
        {%- for block in section.blocks -%}{%- if block.type == 'value' -%}
          {%- if block.settings.lime -%}{%- assign card_class = 'rd-card rd-stamp rd-lime rd-reveal' -%}{%- else -%}{%- assign card_class = 'rd-card rd-stamp rd-reveal' -%}{%- endif -%}
          <div class="{{ card_class }}" {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>
            {%- if block.settings.image_pic != blank -%}
              <div class="rd-val-media">
                <img src="{{ block.settings.image_pic | image_url: width: 900 }}" srcset="{{ block.settings.image_pic | image_url: width: 480 }} 480w, {{ block.settings.image_pic | image_url: width: 900 }} 900w" sizes="(max-width:900px) 92vw, 380px" alt="{{ block.settings.image_alt | escape }}" loading="lazy" width="{{ block.settings.image_pic.width }}" height="{{ block.settings.image_pic.height }}">
              </div>
            {%- elsif block.settings.image != blank -%}
              <div class="rd-val-media">
                {%- if block.settings.image contains '//' -%}
                  <img src="{{ block.settings.image }}&width=900" srcset="{{ block.settings.image }}&width=480 480w, {{ block.settings.image }}&width=900 900w" sizes="(max-width:900px) 92vw, 380px" alt="{{ block.settings.image_alt | escape }}" loading="lazy" width="900" height="563">
                {%- else -%}
                  <img src="{{ block.settings.image | asset_url }}" alt="{{ block.settings.image_alt | escape }}" loading="lazy" width="900" height="563">
                {%- endif -%}
              </div>
            {%- endif -%}
            <div class="rd-body">
              {%- if block.settings.tag != blank -%}<span class="rd-tag rd-lime">{{ block.settings.tag }}</span>{%- endif -%}
              <h3 class="rd-mt2 rd-fs-21px">{{ block.settings.title }}</h3>
              {%- if block.settings.body != blank -%}<p>{{ block.settings.body }}</p>{%- endif -%}
              {%- if block.settings.evidence != blank -%}<p class="rd-val-ev">{{ block.settings.evidence }}</p>{%- endif -%}
            </div>
          </div>
        {%- endif -%}{%- endfor -%}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  {%- comment -%} Stories band — now the shared snippet (2026-08-01). Was an inline copy;
     moving it to snippets/bbc-stories-band.liquid means the lead-card layout and any
     future card change reach all seven story-carrying pages at once. {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- render 'bbc-stories-band', section: section -%}

  {%- comment -%} ---------- RECOGNITION (press logos + stats) ---------- {%- endcomment -%}
  <section class="rd-pad-sm rd-steel">
    <div class="rd-wrap rd-center">
      {%- comment -%} press strip — THE standard block (qa/PRESS-BLOCK.md);
         replaced the per-block grid + its styled-TEXT fallbacks (real logos only) {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- render 'bbc-press',
          style: 'quiet',
          preset: 'national',
          label: section.settings.press_eyebrow,
          more_label: section.settings.press_more,
          more_url: section.settings.press_more_url -%}

      {%- comment -%} recognition & exhibitions — vault rule: separate from earned press {%- endcomment -%}
      <div class="rd-mt4">
        {%- render 'bbc-press', style: 'quiet', preset: 'recognition', label: 'recognition & exhibitions' -%}
      </div>

      {%- assign stat_blocks = section.blocks | where: 'type', 'stat' -%}
      {%- if stat_blocks.size > 0 -%}
        {%- comment -%} DEVICE C — dimension callouts. .rd-dim is an OPT-IN modifier because
           .rd-stats is shared by 12 sections. It draws each figure on a dimension line with
           extension ticks, which promotes the `source` field from small print to the datum
           note a drawing would actually carry. {%- endcomment -%}
        <div class="rd-stats rd-dim rd-mt4">
          {%- for block in stat_blocks -%}
            <div class="rd-stat rd-reveal" {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>
              <span class="rd-dimt" aria-hidden="true"></span>
              <div class="rd-num bbc-counted">{{ block.settings.number }}</div>
              <div class="rd-lbl">{{ block.settings.label }}</div>
              {%- if block.settings.source != blank -%}<div class="rd-src">{{ block.settings.source }}</div>{%- endif -%}
            </div>
          {%- endfor -%}
        </div>
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>
  </section>

  {%- comment -%} ---------- FINAL CTA ---------- {%- endcomment -%}
  <section class="rd-pad rd-dark rd-center">
    <div class="rd-wrap rd-mw-680px">
      {%- if section.settings.cta_eyebrow != blank -%}<span class="rd-eyebrow rd-on-dark">{{ section.settings.cta_eyebrow }}</span>{%- endif -%}
      <h2 class="rd-reveal">{{ section.settings.cta_title }}</h2>
      {%- if section.settings.cta_lede != blank -%}<p class="rd-lede rd-mt2 rd-mx-auto">{{ section.settings.cta_lede }}</p>{%- endif -%}
      <div class="rd-flex rd-mt3 rd-jc-center">
        {%- if section.settings.cta1_label != blank -%}<a class="rd-btn rd-lime" href="{{ cta1 }}">{{ section.settings.cta1_label }} <span class="rd-arrow">&rarr;</span></a>{%- endif -%}
        {%- if section.settings.cta2_label != blank -%}<a class="rd-btn rd-on-dark" href="{{ cta2 }}">{{ section.settings.cta2_label }}</a>{%- endif -%}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

</div>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "About 2026 (new design)",
  "tag": "section",
  "class": "section bbc-about-2026-wrap",
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Hero"
    },
    {
      "type": "image_picker",
      "id": "hero_image",
      "label": "Hero image"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "hero_fallback",
      "label": "Default hero photo filename",
      "default": "bbc-rd-cohort.jpg"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "hero_image_alt",
      "label": "Hero image alt text",
      "default": "A group of builders with their finished bamboo bikes and build plans"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "crumb_home_label",
      "label": "Breadcrumb: home label",
      "default": "Home"
    },
    {
      "type": "url",
      "id": "crumb_home_url",
      "label": "Breadcrumb: home link (defaults to /)"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "crumb_here",
      "label": "Breadcrumb: current page",
      "default": "Our Story"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "hero_eyebrow",
      "label": "Eyebrow",
      "default": "Our story"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "hero_title",
      "label": "Headline",
      "default": "it started with one frame and a stubborn idea."
    },
    {
      "type": "textarea",
      "id": "hero_lede",
      "label": "Lede",
      "default": "That anyone — given the right tools and a bit of belief — can build a bicycle. Today, that idea is changing lives."
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Mission intro"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "intro_eyebrow",
      "label": "Eyebrow",
      "default": "The idea"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "intro_title",
      "label": "Title",
      "default": "we believe building things is powerful."
    },
    {
      "type": "textarea",
      "id": "intro_body_1",
      "label": "Paragraph 1",
      "default": "In 2012, design engineers James Marr and Ian McMillan opened a small workshop in Hackney with a single goal: prove that anyone can build a bicycle frame. They started with bamboo — a fast-growing grass you can shape with hand tools."
    },
    {
      "type": "textarea",
      "id": "intro_body_2",
      "label": "Paragraph 2",
      "default": "What began as a maker's hobby became something bigger. Today the same craft runs inside prisons, schools and community workshops — turning a bike into a route to skills, confidence and a second chance."
    },
    {
      "type": "textarea",
      "id": "intro_quote",
      "label": "Pull quote",
      "default": "If we want people to choose sustainable options, we need to offer something better than what polluting products can be."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "intro_cite",
      "label": "Quote attribution",
      "default": "James Marr, Founder"
    },
    {
      "type": "image_picker",
      "id": "intro_image_pic",
      "label": "Origin photo — a founder working, not posed"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "intro_image",
      "label": "…or image filename / full URL",
      "default": "https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0502/8695/2631/files/JamesMarr.jpg?v=1701273981"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "intro_image_alt",
      "label": "Origin photo alt text",
      "default": "James Marr drilling a bamboo tube held in a jig, in the Bamboo Bicycle Club workshop"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "intro_caption",
      "label": "Origin photo caption",
      "default": "James Marr at the bench — he still teaches every cohort."
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Timeline (add rows below as Milestone blocks)"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "tl_eyebrow",
      "label": "Eyebrow",
      "default": "The journey"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "tl_title",
      "label": "Title",
      "default": "fourteen years, one through-line."
    },
    {
      "type": "textarea",
      "id": "tl_intro",
      "label": "Intro",
      "default": "Every chapter widened who gets to build — and the mission grew naturally out of the craft, not bolted on beside it."
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "The model (split + funding loop)"
    },
    {
      "type": "image_picker",
      "id": "model_image",
      "label": "Image (workshop, no identifiable learners)"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "model_fallback",
      "label": "Default model photo filename",
      "default": "bbc-rd-workshop.jpg"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "model_image_alt",
      "label": "Image alt text",
      "default": "Inside the bamboo bicycle workshop"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "model_eyebrow",
      "label": "Eyebrow",
      "default": "How we're built"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "model_title",
      "label": "Title",
      "default": "a shop and a mission, one engine."
    },
    {
      "type": "textarea",
      "id": "model_body",
      "label": "Body",
      "default": "We're a Community Interest Company — not a charity with a gift shop. The money flows in one loop."
    },
